WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.526
Several ablations show why CoCN works.

00:00:03.606 --> 00:00:07.131
First, permutation heads matter: with more permutations,

00:00:07.211 --> 00:00:10.737
accuracy rises consistently on MUTAG, Chameleon,
Cornell, and Wisconsin,

00:00:10.817 --> 00:00:14.342
since each exposes different node arrangements.

00:00:14.422 --> 00:00:17.948
Second, larger diagonal kernels give a bigger
receptive field and better performance,

00:00:18.028 --> 00:00:21.553
without over-smoothing.

00:00:21.633 --> 00:00:25.159
Third,

00:00:25.239 --> 00:00:28.764
an information-loss study finds the relaxed
permutations preserve almost all information,

00:00:28.844 --> 00:00:32.370
so the regularization is lossless.
